## DO

- Assume Python 3.12, src layout, line length 100.
- Add tests alongside new rules/bug fixes whenever possible.
- Handle API keys/secrets only via `.env` or config boundaries; never hardcode.
- When verification not run, report commands not executed, reason, remaining risk.
- If `black .` modifies files, report formatting changes + verification results.

## DON'T

- No I/O, UI, DB, external API calls in domain.
- No application import of concrete adapter implementations.
- No business policy in adapters.
- No reporting commands as passed when unverified.
- No implementation while plan unapproved.
- No diff inflation via renames differing only by leading underscore, e.g. `func`↔`_func` ([`shapez2-core.mdc`](mdc:.cursor/rules/shapez2-core.mdc) Forbidden Shortcuts).

